<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 9 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">India through the Ages</h1><p class="path-tagline">From Ashoka's edicts to the Marathas: the subcontinent's great powers in sequence.</p><p class="path-intro">Few lands have carried so many great states as the Indian subcontinent. This path moves through them in order: the Mauryan empire that first united the subcontinent and the emperor who renounced war; the classical age of the Guptas; the sultans of Delhi; the glittering south of Vijayanagara; the Mughal zenith and its monuments; and the Maratha confederacy that supplanted it.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Timekeeper</a> · <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/maurya-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Profile · 322 BCE – 185 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Maurya Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">The first empire to span the subcontinent, with a bureaucracy ahead of its time.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashoka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Person · d. 232 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Ashoka</span><span class="path-step-why">The conqueror of Kalinga who turned to dhamma and carved his conscience onto rocks and pillars.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/gupta-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abhijnanasakuntalam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Profile · 240 CE – 550 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Gupta Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">The classical age: mathematics, poetry and temple art under a light imperial hand.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qutb-minar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Profile · 1206 CE – 1526 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Delhi Sultanate</span><span class="path-step-why">Three centuries of sultans who made Delhi one of the great capitals of the Islamic world.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vedas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Profile · 1336 CE – 1646 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Vijayanagara Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">The city of victory that ruled the south and awed every traveller who saw it.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/mughal-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-mahal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Profile · 1526 CE – 1857 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Mughal Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">From Babur to Aurangzeb: the richest empire on earth in its day.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/akbar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akbar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Person · r. 1556–1605</span><span class="path-step-name">Akbar</span><span class="path-step-why">The Mughal who ruled by inclusion, debating every faith at his court.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/taj-mahal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-mahal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · Work</span><span class="path-step-name">Taj Mahal</span><span class="path-step-why">Grief in white marble: the empire's wealth and craft in one building.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/maratha-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shivaji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">9 · Profile · 1674 CE – 1818 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Maratha Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">The confederacy that broke Mughal power and dominated eighteenth-century India.</span></span></a></li></ol>
